    "description": "Record a decision the user needs to make, so it is tracked in their Decisions pane instead of getting lost in the chat. Use it whenever you need the user to choose between approaches, confirm an assumption, or supply information you cannot infer, and you can keep working meanwhile (on other parts, or on a stated default). Returns a reference like D3. Mention that reference in your reply. The user answers in the pane; the answer arrives as a note in a later tool result or prompt, naming the reference. Once every decision raised in one turn is answered and you are idle, you are prompted to carry on. Do not raise the same question twice; check the open list this tool returns. If the user settles a decision in the chat instead of the pane, call close_decision so it leaves their open list."
